In this solution, the `XmlFileParser` class reads an XML file from a file and parses its elements. It removes any XML declaration that may be present at the beginning of the file.

The `main` method creates an instance of the `XmlFileParser` class, reads the XML file from it, and then calls the `parse` method to parse the XML.

This solution uses a simple parsing approach based on string splitting. It assumes that each element is represented by one or more lines of content enclosed in opening tags (e.g., `<tag>Text</tag>`).
